# Always revalidate CSS/JS/images/PDFs so edits propagate without stale caches.
# pdf was missing here until 2026-08-03, and it mattered: the sample report was
# corrected twice and the live site kept serving the superseded file to anyone
# following the bare link, while ?v= links got the new one. A cached stylesheet
# looks wrong. A cached PDF is a document going out with defects we already fixed.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(css|js|png|jpg|jpeg|gif|svg|ico|webp|pdf)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>

# The "Leak Finder" was renamed "Gap Finder" (2026-07-31). Anything already
# linking to the old URLs — an email, a QR code, a prospect's bookmark —
# still lands in the right place.
Redirect 301 /leak-finder-demo.html /gap-finder-demo.html
Redirect 301 /leak-map-demo.html /gap-map-demo.html
Redirect 301 /assets/leak-quiz.js /assets/gap-quiz.js

# A local homepage review copy was deployed by accident. Removing it from the
# repo is NOT enough — this host adds and updates files on deploy but never
# deletes them, so it stayed live at 200 with index,follow and the homepage's
# full content. Redirect it away, which also consolidates anything that linked
# to it. Any future *-review.html copy is covered by the same rule.
Redirect 301 /home-centered-review.html /
RedirectMatch 301 ^/.+-review\.html$ /

# Two industry pages covered categories that already had a page: "Bars &
# Restaurants" against "Restaurants & Bars", and "Dental & Medical" against
# "Medical & Dental". They were never in the nav, the footer or the sitemap, so
# nothing linked them but the thank-you page, and near-duplicate pages competing
# for the same terms help nobody. Consolidated into the surviving twin. Deleting
# the files is not enough here, same as the review copy above: this host never
# removes a file on deploy, so without these rules both stay live at 200.
Redirect 301 /industry-bars.html /industry-restaurants.html
Redirect 301 /industry-dental.html /industry-medical-dental.html

# Keep internal planning docs private: no HTTP access, no directory listing.
Options -Indexes
RedirectMatch 404 ^/docs(/|$)
RedirectMatch 404 ^/.+\.(md)$
RedirectMatch 404 ^/demo/_archive(/|$)
